WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.567
Pick a class and ride it. Telo Ride now has the class ride screen, driving the bike

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:08.888
through the plan.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:14.771
The header names the class and the mode, with the clock as a timer: seven minutes of

00:00:14.771 --> 00:00:15.442
thirty.

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:25.120
The segment card counts down the part you're in: its kind, its time left, its

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.105
progress, and the whole plan.

00:00:30.971 --> 00:00:35.450
Power reads against the segment's target. Within ten percent it's on target;

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.341
otherwise it shows the gap.

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:46.024
The stepper shows the resistance the bike reports, or a dash. Plus and minus nudge

00:00:46.024 --> 00:00:48.689
it, and switch off when the bike is away.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.503
At each boundary the next level goes to the bike. After a long gap, only the current

00:00:56.503 --> 00:00:57.617
level is sent.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.551
The class comes from the catalogue: one request, and the ride starts the moment it

00:01:06.551 --> 00:01:07.301
arrives.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:17.489
The first HTTP client costs about five kilobytes on the wire, so the bundle budget

00:01:17.489 --> 00:01:18.936
makes room for it.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:29.651
Still to come: the video in sync in 5.3, pause, leave or finish in 5.4, and the

00:01:29.651 --> 00:01:31.828
catalogue API in 6.1.

00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:38.116
On a phone the panel stacks in two columns. From tablet width, it's one row of four.

00:01:43.237 --> 00:01:47.656
What the tests prove: four new specs drive the screen on a fake clock and a fake

00:01:47.656 --> 00:01:49.668
bike, and every check is green.

00:01:53.561 --> 00:01:58.164
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:03.021
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:02:03.021 --> 00:02:04.692
every hill and interval.

00:02:05.037 --> 00:02:10.215
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:02:10.215 --> 00:02:15.663
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:02:15.663 --> 00:02:18.653
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:02:18.998 --> 00:02:21.491
A custom workout lives under Profile.
